\vspace{0.22cm}
{\Large\bfseries\color{ChapterCedar} 全書一句話 \textperiodcentered\ The Whole Book in One Verse}

\vspace{0.30cm}
\fcolorbox{ScriptureGold}{ScriptureBg}{%
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\centering\vspace{0.2cm}
\normalsize\color{CommentaryBrown}
然而耶和華─他的　神因大衛的緣故，仍使他在耶路撒冷有\textbf{\color{LampAmber!80!black}燈光}，叫他兒子接續他作王，堅立耶路撒冷。\\[0.5em]
\footnotesize\itshape
But for David's sake the LORD his God gave him a \textbf{lamp} in Jerusalem, to raise up his son after him and to establish Jerusalem;\\[0.4em]
\small\color{ChapterCedar} 列王紀上 15:4 \textperiodcentered\ 1 Kings 15:4
\vspace{0.2cm}
\end{minipage}}

\vspace{0.35cm}
{\small\color{TextGray} 二十二章經文 \textperiodcentered\ 二十四個研讀單元 \textperiodcentered\ 八卷 \textperiodcentered\ 殿會舊，國會裂，王會倒，燈卻長有\\
\textit{Twenty-two chapters \textperiodcentered\ twenty-four study units \textperiodcentered\ eight volumes \textperiodcentered\ the house grows old, the kingdom splits, the kings fall; the lamp stays}}

\vspace{0.30cm}
{\small
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.3}
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{2.8cm}p{2.4cm}p{6.9cm}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{段落} & \textbf{王上章節} & \textbf{在全書的展開} \\
\midrule
所羅門的王國 & 1-11章 & 起誓登基、求智慧、建殿獻殿——榮光升到最高；然後第二次顯現的警告、最後的判決，一盞燈留了下來 \\
分裂的王國 & 12-16章 & 示劍之會裂國，金牛犢取代聖殿，先知的話代替王的詔令；王朝像骨牌一樣更迭 \\
以利亞與亞哈 & 17-22章 & 乾旱、迦密山、何烈山的微小聲音；拿伯的葡萄園；一支隨便射出的箭 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
}

\vspace{0.4cm}
\textcolor{ScriptureGold}{\rule{2.5in}{0.7pt}}
\vspace{0.3cm}

{\bfseries\color{ChapterCedar} 讀經之鑰 \textperiodcentered\ How to Read This Book}

\vspace{0.18cm}
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\small\color{TextGray}
不是來讀一部「帝國興衰史」，是來看一件事：殿蓋成了，榮光充滿了，王卻一個一個倒下去——
那麼，是甚麼留了下來？\\
若你讀完二十二章卻只記得「所羅門很有智慧」——請從頭再讀，\\
這次留意：神四次向所羅門說話（賜與、建殿之中、警告、判決），每一次，「大衛」的名字都沒有缺席；
這卷書的空缺，正是留給你去問：那盞燈最後點在誰身上？\\[0.5em]
\textit{\footnotesize
You are not reading a rise-and-fall chronicle of an empire. You are watching one thing:
the house is finished, the glory fills it, and the kings fall one after another —
so what is it that remains?\\
If after twenty-two chapters you remember only "Solomon was wise," read it again.\\
This time notice: God speaks to Solomon four times (gift, mid-building word, warning, verdict),
and each time David's name is present. The book's open ending asks you:
on whom does that lamp finally burn?}
\end{minipage}

\vfill
{\scriptsize\color{LightGray} PubHub 三書精讀系統 \textperiodcentered\ Soli Deo Gloria}

